{ Welcome to my new study on the French Defense! In my previous studies, I've given you a good opening for white (the London System) and a good defense to 1. d4 for black (the Stonewall Dutch) and now, I'm completing this opening repertoire with the French Defense, a good defense to 1. e4. Please ❤ this study if you would like to see more studies from me! }
1. e4 { We can now play the French Defense with 1. ... e6 (you can play that now). } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Ge7e6] } 1... e6 { This is the French Defense, which has been played by top players since the 1800s. The French has been used by many strong players, including Mikhail Botvinnik, Viktor Korchnoi, Akiba Rubinstein, Aron Nimzowitsch, Tigran Petrosian, and more! The French Defense is easy to learn, and can be played well by players of all levels and playing styles. Black tries to counterattack with 2. ... d5 quickly. Let's explore this fascinating opening! } *

[Event "French Defense: King's Indian Attack"]
[Date "2021.11.06"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "C00"]
[Opening "French Defense: King's Indian Attack"]
[StudyName "French Defense"]
[ChapterName "King's Indian Attack"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/QU8o2AIu/oA4pf0P2"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/caelT8"]
[UTCDate "2021.11.06"]
[UTCTime "15:00:26"]
[Orientation "black"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Before we dive into the main lines of the French, there are some sidelines we need to know. First up, the King's Indian Attack. }
1. e4 { How do we play the French? } 1... e6 2. d3 { This is the King's Indian Attack. White aims to play Nf3, g3, Bg2, 0-0, Nbd2 and then attack with e5 and f4. So, what should we do? Well, in the French, we usually like to counterattack with ... d5. } 2... d5 3. Nd2 { In the French, we also like to play ...c5. } 3... c5 4. Ngf3 { And, let's develop our b8-knight. } 4... Nc6 5. g3 { Now we fianchetto our own bishop to help defend. } 5... g6 6. Bg2 { Now, where should our dark-squared bishop go? } 6... Bg7 7. O-O { Develop our knight to e7. } { [%csl Ge7][%cal Gg8e7] } 7... Nge7 { The point of this line is to stop a critical pawn advance for white, e5. Now that we've stopped it, we can castle kingside, and counterattack on the queenside. We have a good game. } *

[Event "French Defense: Chigorin Variation"]
[Date "2021.11.06"]
[Result "*"]
